🎁 Bonus Learning: Why Can Recursion Be Slow?

The recursive Fibonacci function repeatedly calculates the same values.

For example, calculating fib_recursive(6) requires calculating fib_recursive(4) through more than one path. As n grows, the same smaller calculations are repeated many times.

Try comparing:

fib_recursive(35)
fib_recursive(40)

The recursive version can become much slower as the number increases.

The loop version is more efficient for generating a long Fibonacci series because it calculates each next number once and stores it in a list.

